  <p class="lead">The energy landscape in India is undergoing a massive shift towards sustainability, and the residential rooftop solar sector is leading this charge. The central government's landmark <strong>PM Surya Ghar Muft Bijli Yojna</strong> aims to provide up to 300 free electricity units per month to one crore households. In Uttar Pradesh — and particularly in Lucknow — homeowners are rushing to register, eager to escape rising grid tariffs and tap into generous government subsidies.</p>

  <p>Installing a solar system is, however, a technical process involving structural safety, electrical wiring, discom approvals, and documentation. That is where professional empanelled vendors like <strong>V.P. Infra Properties (OPC) Private Limited</strong> come in. As a certified empanelled installer, V.P. Infra Properties handles the entire installation lifecycle, so you can claim your subsidy with confidence. In this guide, we break down the scheme's rules, the subsidy amounts, the application steps, and what you can expect from the process.</p>

  <h2>Understanding the Double-Subsidy Model for Lucknow</h2>

  <p>One of the primary reasons for the scheme's rapid adoption is the double-subsidy model available to UP residents. When you install a residential grid-tied solar system in Lucknow, you are eligible for both <strong>Central Financial Assistance (CFA)</strong> from the national government and a bonus <strong>State Subsidy</strong> from the Government of Uttar Pradesh.</p>

  <h3>Central Government Subsidies (CFA)</h3>
  <p>The central government provides a direct benefit transfer based on installed capacity:</p>

  <table class="data-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Solar Capacity</th>
        <th>Suitable For (Monthly Units)</th>
        <th>Central Subsidy (Rs.)</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>1 kW</td>
        <td>Up to 150 units</td>
        <td>Rs. 30,000</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>2 kW</td>
        <td>150 – 300 units</td>
        <td>Rs. 60,000</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>3 kW or above</td>
        <td>More than 300 units</td>
        <td>Rs. 78,000 (Maximum)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Uttar Pradesh State Government Bonus Subsidy</h3>
  <p>UPNEDA (Uttar Pradesh New and Renewable Energy Development Agency) adds a further <strong>Rs. 15,000 per kW, capped at Rs. 30,000</strong> for domestic consumers. For a 3 kW+ system this means:</p>

  <div class="note-box">
    <strong>Total Combined Subsidy for 3 kW system in Lucknow:</strong><br/>
    Rs. 78,000 (Central) + Rs. 30,000 (State UP) = <strong>Rs. 1,08,000</strong>
  </div>

  <h2>Why Work with V.P. Infra Properties (OPC) Private Limited?</h2>

  <p>The PM Surya Ghar rules strictly require that installation be carried out by a vendor <strong>empanelled on the national portal</strong>. Using an unregistered contractor means forfeiting all subsidies.</p>

  <p><strong>V.P. Infra Properties (OPC) Private Limited</strong> is an ISO 9001:2015 certified, empanelled solar installer headquartered in Lucknow. We manage every step so you never have to navigate the bureaucracy alone:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Technical Site Survey:</strong> Roof inspection, shadow analysis, wind-load checks, and system-sizing matched to your electricity bills.</li>
    <li><strong>Portal Assistance:</strong> End-to-end help with document uploads, discom coordination, and application submission on the national solar portal.</li>
