  <h2>Eligibility Criteria for Lucknow Homeowners</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Active electricity connection with a <strong>domestic residential tariff</strong> (MVVNL/UPPCL consumer).</li>
    <li>Ownership of a house with a concrete, shadow-free roof.</li>
    <li>No prior solar subsidy claimed under any other government scheme for the same premises.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Step-by-Step Application & Installation Process</h2>

  <ol class="steps-list">
    <li>
      <strong>Register on the National Portal</strong> — Create an account using your mobile number, email, state (Uttar Pradesh), discom (MVVNL), and consumer account number from your electricity bill.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Apply for Technical Feasibility</strong> — Submit an online application. Discom engineers verify whether the local transformer can absorb the solar export. V.P. Infra guides you throughout.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Execute Installation</strong> — Once feasibility is approved, we sign the installation agreement and proceed with the full system setup at your site.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Discom Inspection & Net Meter</strong> — We upload completion photos and a work report. Discom officers inspect the plant and install the bi-directional net meter.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Subsidy Bank Transfer</strong> — After net-meter commissioning, you submit your bank details on the portal. The combined subsidy is credited directly within 30 days.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Financial ROI: What Does It Really Cost You?</h2>

  <p>For a standard <strong>3 kW On-Grid Solar System</strong> in Lucknow:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Gross Cost:</strong> Rs. 1,60,000 – Rs. 1,75,000 (depending on module type and site complexity).</li>
    <li><strong>Total Subsidy:</strong> Rs. 1,08,000 (Central + State UP).</li>
    <li><strong>Net Out-of-Pocket Cost:</strong> Rs. 52,000 – Rs. 67,000.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>A 3 kW system generates roughly <strong>12–14 units per day</strong> — about 4,500 units annually. At Lucknow's average domestic tariff of Rs. 7 per unit, this saves approximately <strong>Rs. 31,500 per year</strong>. With a net investment of ~Rs. 60,000, the payback period is just <strong>under 2 years</strong>. With panels warranted for 25 years, you enjoy clean, virtually free electricity for the remaining 23 years.</p>

